{"id": "EUVD-2026-86244", "enisaUuid": "784c1a00-643b-314b-af76-5c1bde07bb5e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/vfio-ap: fix potential use of uninitialized apm_filtered bitmap\n\nThe DECLARE_BITMAP(apm_filtered, AP_DEVICES) macro allocates the bitmap\non the stack without zero-initializing it.\n\nIn vfio_ap_mdev_hot_plug_cfg(), the vfio_ap_mdev_filter_matrix() function\nis only called to initialize and populate apm_filtered if either\nfilter_adapters or filter_domains is true. If the hot plug configuration\nchange only adds control domains (meaning filter_cdoms is true, but\nfilter_adapters and filter_domains are both false),\nvfio_ap_mdev_filter_matrix() is bypassed.\n\nConsequently, apm_filtered is passed to reset_queues_for_apids() with\nuninitialized stack garbage. This can cause reset_queues_for_apids() to\ninterpret arbitrary stack garbage bits as valid APIDs to reset, potentially\nperforming unintended guest hardware queue resets.\n\nFix this by zero-initializing the apm_filtered bitmap at the beginning of\nvfio_ap_mdev_hot_plug_cfg() using bitmap_zero().", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:34:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:07:49", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ba8a08f5f26ed59f356a6318bca3aa7cc0af3e2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f73db632524320d2b93bc8534be8ea875053502d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d554f2571e6b4db242593ba561efd6a6d1f99a9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09548edc6114f1eb1035b30795e893204ef45b85", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf09b9d7cd7890bc3a3b7eb63d5ece15f88bfde7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q4pw-hxg7-r6v7", "CVE-2026-93238"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0afce1ff-7fe3-344f-a7a4-a5f220d30398", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "283c0e63-869d-3565-b76f-7925b5ab1ab0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "5eb431c5-1859-31f4-9295-17d32b4d8dd5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eeb386aeb5b7c8d2dae6a3ba49255d8a97803182 <4ba8a08f5f26ed59f356a6318bca3aa7cc0af3e2"}, {"id": "5ffe0686-010a-374a-80b1-f367101467f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "95c172e8-51d3-3ee2-b1e9-cf9c5f5fa98a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "a13976bd-0552-3fe6-b983-ce78528df6b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eeb386aeb5b7c8d2dae6a3ba49255d8a97803182 <09548edc6114f1eb1035b30795e893204ef45b85"}, {"id": "ac333608-d5fb-3ee9-866f-6efea1e6643b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eeb386aeb5b7c8d2dae6a3ba49255d8a97803182 <bf09b9d7cd7890bc3a3b7eb63d5ece15f88bfde7"}, {"id": "c144b8b9-a23f-37e8-84c0-74361779548f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eeb386aeb5b7c8d2dae6a3ba49255d8a97803182 <f73db632524320d2b93bc8534be8ea875053502d"}, {"id": "d15dcfed-1398-376f-a48a-cff03d9cd35b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e8a43839-0d4b-3976-aafd-1e2a5498d8a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "edefd68d-6fa5-3f50-9687-c7c220455077", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "f0f95457-0cd2-36bc-b73d-81604dab39e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eeb386aeb5b7c8d2dae6a3ba49255d8a97803182 <6d554f2571e6b4db242593ba561efd6a6d1f99a9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0b9143af-5751-3478-9a67-ec164f901e0b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}